   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package initializer for the `exllamav3` library. Its main job is to import PyTorch up front and raise a helpful, actionable error if it's missing \u2014 since the package intentionally doesn't install torch automatically (because the correct torch build depends on the user's CUDA setup), it points users to installation instructions instead. It then applies default CUDA allocator settings (enabling expandable segments unless the user has configured the allocator themselves, skipped on Windows or unsupported torch builds), and finally exposes the library's public API by importing key classes like `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `Cache`, `Generator`, and sampler utilities."
  },
  "8192": {
