   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "f8a24adafd5b2161676fa1838801f2f1bef48f78c653565dfedc6574fb571396",
   "text": "The first three files, in order of appearance, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package initializer for the exllamav3 library. Its main job is to verify that PyTorch is installed before anything else runs \u2014 since exllamav3 intentionally does not declare torch as a default dependency (because the correct torch build depends on the user's CUDA setup), it raises a helpful error message with installation instructions if the import fails. It then applies default CUDA caching allocator settings (enabling expandable segments) unless the user has already configured the allocator themselves, has set the `EXL3_EXPANDABLE_SEGMENTS` environment variable to disable it, or is on Windows where the feature isn't reliably supported. Finally, it exposes the library's public API by importing key classes such as `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `Cache`, `Generator`, and sampler components."
  }
